    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**Core logic** \u2014 `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`:\n- Now derives `CITY3` (upper-cased first 3 letters of city) and `LAST3` (upper-cased first 3 of lastName), joined with a per-city 4-digit sequence.\n- The sequence is `one more than the owners already in that city`, counted from `ownerRepository.findAll()` filtered by matching city (case-insensitive), consistent with the same-transaction counting pattern used by `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`.\n- Extracted a small shared `prefix(...)` helper since both CITY3 and LAST3 use identical \"upper-cased first three letters\" logic, avoiding duplication.\n\n**Derived values rebuild automatically:** `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is `<customerCode>-M<YY>` \u2014 it reads the stored `customerCode` value, so it now emits e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26` with no code change needed.\n\n**Documentation kept in sync** with the new format:\n- The `assignCustomerCode` step comment in `owners.POST.yml`\n- The `membershipNumber` Javadoc example in `OwnerMapper.java`\n- The `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml`\n\nThe new acceptance test (`customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass green.",
